{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "sedimentation_upwind1_flux_D_lev_interior",
    "description": "INTERIOR layers k = 1 .. NLEV-1 of the conservative first-order DONOR-CELL divergence of a downward hydrometeor flux on column_nonuniform_1d: (d/dz (W q))[k] = (W[k+1] q[k+1] - W[k] q[k]) / dz[k]. Both the transported density q (rho times a mixing ratio, or any layer quantity) and the velocity W are LAYER-centred ([lev]); W is the signed velocity along +lev (upward), so a fall speed v_t enters as W = -v_t <= 0. Because the flow is downward everywhere, the upstream (donor) cell of face k -- the lower edge of layer k -- is layer k itself, so the flux through face k is F_k = W[k] q[k], carried at the falling layer's OWN speed: exactly the structure of a sedimentation scheme, in which the mass leaving a layer falls at that layer's mass-weighted terminal velocity. Adjacent layers reuse the identical face expression, so the divergence TELESCOPES: sum_k dz[k] (d/dz (W q))[k] = F_{NLEV+1} - F_1 = -F_1, the surface outflow, and the column mass budget closes to round-off (the surface precipitation rate is -F_1 = v_t[1] q[1]). Valid only for W <= 0: for a velocity that changes sign the donor cell changes side and a face-velocity upwind rule (latlon3d upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc) is needed instead. `dz` is the free-name layer thickness of grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm. First order (O(dz)), monotone and positivity-preserving.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "op:advection",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:2",
      "scheme:upwind"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Section 4.1 (the upwind / donor-cell flux)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., & Lim, J.-O. J. (2006). The WRF single-moment 6-class microphysics scheme (WSM6). Journal of the Korean Meteorological Society, 42(2), 129-151."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Juang, H.-M. H., & Hong, S.-Y. (2010). Forward semi-Lagrangian advection with mass conservation and positive definiteness for falling hydrometeors. Monthly Weather Review, 138(5), 1778-1791.",
        "doi": "10.1175/2009MWR3109.1"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "sedimentation_upwind1_flux_D_lev_interior": {
      "params": [
        "q",
        "W"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "aggregate",
        "output_idx": [
          "k"
        ],
        "args": [
          "q",
          "W"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "k": [
            1,
            {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
                "NLEV",
                1
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "W",
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "q",
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            "k",
                            1
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "W",
                        "k"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "q",
                        "k"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "dz",
                "k"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}